From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Kleinschmidt <jkleinsc@electronjs.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: feat: let TracingControllerImpl start from a perfetto config

Adds TracingControllerImpl::StartTracingWithPerfettoConfig(), which
starts a tracing session from a perfetto::TraceConfig the caller
assembled itself. Electron uses it to record Chromium's trace-scoped
native heap profiler data source in the same session as the rest of
the trace, rather than running a second perfetto::TracingSession.

The output format follows the config. If its data sources set
convert_to_legacy_json the session behaves as before; otherwise the
trace is delivered as raw protobuf, read with ReadBuffers() once
OnTracingDisabled() has arrived so that data sources which emit their
final samples while being disabled are included.

The file endpoint is also switched to binary mode so protobuf traces
are not corrupted on Windows.

This matches the upstream CL
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8433288
and can be removed once that lands.

